            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Later Life and Works</strong><br>\nIn his later years, Leopardi's work became even more reflective and critical of contemporary Italy. His disillusionment with the political situation of his country colored his later poems and writings.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Final Years and Death</strong><br>\nLeopardi spent the last years of his life in Naples, where he hoped the climate would improve his health. He died of edema on June 14, 1837, at the age of 38.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy</strong><br>\nLeopardi's legacy lies in his profound impact on Italian literature and the existential depth of his poetry. His work continues to be studied and revered for its beauty and philosophical depth.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
